        {"source": "spec", "quote": "netlist shows 5 column + 7 row lines wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins (matrix scanned by the module itself, not via an onboard keyboard controller)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The seventh keyboard row is never scanned by the module, so every key in that row is non-functional; the QWERTY matrix is incomplete.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the build matches the specification (reference designators are simply renumbered, the FAN53610/EPD-boost values and the barrel-jack battery-disconnect note are correct, and the RJ45 is now wired, resolving the spec's open item). The one deviation I can read off the drawing is that the keyboard's ROW7 net (NET0019) terminates only on U6 and is not connected to any SKW92A pin, leaving one matrix row open."
}

